<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximilian von Montgelas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1759">1759</a>–<a href="/years/1838">1838</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Count Montgelas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maximilian von Montgelas was a Bavarian statesman who, as chief minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-joseph-of-bavaria">Maximilian IV Joseph</a>, later King Maximilian I, from 1799 to 1817, created the modern Bavarian state. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, he greatly enlarged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>'s territory and saw it become a kingdom in 1806, then centralised the administration, secularised monasteries, curbed noble privileges and introduced religious toleration. His reforms prepared the way for the constitution of 1818.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximilian-von-montgelas.jpg" alt="Maximilian von Montgelas" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Hauber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maximilian_von_Montgelas_(1806).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
